cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these results, please cite the article and this archive."
type: software
title: "Views or instants: reproducibility archive for frame-budget allocation in multi-camera path-length measurement"
version: "1.0.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22784740"
abstract: "Analysis code, frozen protocols, input digests, sealed predictions and scored results for a study of how a fixed camera-frame budget should be divided between simultaneous views and time instants when measuring the path length of a moving target. No third-party datasets and no model weights are redistributed; see NOTICE.md."
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jun-Jason-Ji/views-or-instants"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - vision-based measurement
  - distance travelled
  - trajectory length
  - multi-camera triangulation
  - sampling design
  - measurement uncertainty
  - budget allocation
